    [BugFix][Misc] Make Ascend skills explicit-only and streamline agent guidance (#18854)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    The model-adapter and release-management skills currently allow
    automatic invocation when a conversation matches their descriptions.
    Require explicit invocation, and keep always-loaded agent guidance
    focused on the current task.
    
    - Add `policy.allow_implicit_invocation: false` in each skill's
    `agents/openai.yaml` for
    [Codex](https://developers.openai.com/codex/skills/).
    - Set `disable-model-invocation: true` in both skill frontmatters for
    [Claude Code](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/skills),
    [Cursor](https://cursor.com/docs/skills), and [Kimi
    Code](https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code-cli/customization/skills.html).
    - Apply the [Astra prompting
    guidance](https://learn.chatgpt.com/blog/rethinking-skills-and-prompts-for-gpt-6-astra):
    link to relevant documentation when needed, scope validation to the
    change, describe review evidence in the PR, and remove repeated examples
    and setup/check sequences.
    - Append PR testing requirements and a submission checklist to the
    existing testing guide. Link directly to the CI title check, and retain
    NPU hardware validation before merge.
    - Correct the blanket prohibition on model files to reflect the existing
    `vllm_ascend.models` registration path. Link to the patch guide instead
    of repeating an obsolete patch example, and remove misleading NPU
    synchronization examples.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. Both skills require explicit invocation: `$skill-name` in Codex,
    `/skill-name` in Claude Code and Cursor, or `/skill:skill-name` in Kimi
    Code. Existing skill instructions are preserved. Agent guidance now
    routes PR validation to the testing guide and reflects the repository's
    existing model registration patterns.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `bash format.sh ci`: all checks passed. The repository excludes
    `.agents/` from pre-commit, so the metadata was also checked separately.
    - Parsed the skill frontmatters and `agents/openai.yaml` files with
    PyYAML; verified boolean invocation settings and confirmed that the
    original descriptions and skill bodies are unchanged.
    - Codex app-server `skills/list` discovered both repository skills as
    enabled. This checks discovery only; the response does not expose
    invocation policy. Per-client model-inference end-to-end tests were not
    run.
    - Rendered `AGENTS.md` and the testing guide and checked relative links
    and section anchors. Verified that the complete original testing-guide
    content is preserved and the new section is appended.
    - Verified the model-registration guidance against
    `vllm_ascend/models/__init__.py` and the plugin registration entry
    point. Checked the current PR title using the workflow's `grep -iqE`
    pattern.
    - Reviewed the instruction changes against the Astra guide. No
    model-quality improvement is claimed without behavioral evaluations. No
    vLLM runtime code changed.
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c4df37dfcc7f72ca41cd43801a468526ecf99a2b
    
    Signed-off-by: maoxx241 <maomaoyu870@gmail.com>

